## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design edge routing with policy-driven gating and cross-DC deployment, plus observability and security concerns in docker-dca.

## Key Concepts

- TLS termination at the edge with Nginx
- Central policy engine (OPA) integration
- Per-tenant feature flag evaluation
- Cross-DC routing semantics
- Observability with Prometheus and OTEL

## Code Example

```rego
package featureflag.allow
default allow = false
allow {
  input.tenant == "tenant-A"
  input.flag == "new_feature"
}
```

```nginx
# Nginx map-based routing example
http {
  map $http_x_feature_flag $upstream {
    default http://api_v1;
    "new_feature" http://api_v2;
  }
  server {
    listen 443 ssl;
    location /api/ { proxy_pass $upstream; }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you implement cache invalidation for policy decisions?
- How would you test the canary routing?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical ability to add non-intrusive QA in production, teaches traffic manipulation without risking user impact, and validates multi-DC deployment awareness.

## Key Concepts
- Traffic shadowing vs canary releases
- Nginx mirror and upstream configuration
- Docker-DC/edge proxy routing across DCs
- TLS edge termination and tenant isolation

## Code Example
```nginx
# Example shadow config snippet
upstream prod_api { server prod-api:8080; }
upstream staging_api { server staging-api:8080; }
server {
  listen 443 ssl;
  location /api/ {
    proxy_pass http://prod_api;
    mirror /mirror_to_staging;
  }
  location = /mirror_to_staging {
    proxy_pass http://staging_api;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you monitor shadowed traffic to ensure no unseen side effects?
- How would you prevent skew if tenant_id headers can be spoofed?

## Why This Is Asked
This tests automation, Vault + SPIFFE integration, and zero-downtime trust reconfiguration across DCs.

## Key Concepts
- Vault CA bundles and SPIFFE trust anchors
- SPIFFE SVID rotation and edge-proxy hot-reload
- Idempotence, rollback, and verification across DCs

## Code Example
```javascript
// bootstrap trust distribution (pseudocode)
async function bootstrapCrossDC(dc) {
  await fetchTrustAnchors(dc);
  await rotateSVIDs(dc);
  await hotReloadProxies(dc);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test drift between trust material and service SVIDs?
- How do you handle partial failures during bootstrap (e.g., one DC unreachable)?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design tenant-aware data residency and policy enforcement in docker-dca, including edge TLS termination, overlay data paths, and canary safety net.

## Key Concepts
- docker-dca multi-DC deployment
- SPIFFE/SVID rotation with Vault
- data residency via overlay networks/volumes
- per-tenant policy with OPA
- canary rollout and rollback criteria

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code illustrating policy check
const tenant = req.headers['x-tenant'];
if (allowedTenants[tenant]?.includes(req.path)) {
  next();
} else {
  res.status(403).send('forbidden');
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you monitor cross-tenant data access to ensure residency is respected?
- How would you test the canary rollback under sudden quota breach?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical knowledge of per-tenant configuration via Docker Config, feature gating, and edge proxy routing in a multi-DC setup.

## Key Concepts
- Docker Config for per-tenant rules
- Feature flag gating in API
- Traefik TLS and docker-dca wiring
- Lightweight bootstrap and config reload

## Code Example
```javascript
// sample Express middleware for feature gate
const fs = require('fs');
let flags = {};
try { flags = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync('/config/feature-flags.json','utf8')); } catch(e) { flags = {}; }
function featureGate(req,res,next){
  const tenant = req.headers['x-tenant'];
  if(!tenant) return res.status(400).send('Missing X-Tenant');
  const enabled = flags[tenant] && flags[tenant].includes('new-feature');
  if(!enabled) return res.status(403).send('Forbidden');
  next();
}
app.get('/new-feature', featureGate, (req,res)=>{ res.send('New feature access granted'); });
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you hot-reload the flags without restarting the API?
- How would you test isolation across tenants when flags change?
